"enText": "These first four days in Athens (雅典) and its port, Piraeus (比雷埃夫斯), read the city as a layered palimpsest (城市層疊). Classical ruins sit inside a Neoclassical (新古典主義) capital rebuilt after 1834: the Corinthian colonnade (科林斯柱廊) of Hadrian's Library stands beside the Monastiraki metro, and the columns of the Temple of Olympian Zeus (奧林匹亞宙斯神殿) show the Roman scale of the classical orders (古典柱式). At Syntagma Square (憲法廣場) the Evzones (總統衛隊) perform a choreographed changing of the guard, while the Little Metropolis (小主教座堂) reuses carved spolia (再利用石材). Everyday design is just as instructive: handwritten price cards at the Central Market (中央市場), graffiti in Psirri (普西里) and the themed façade of Little Kook show vernacular typography (庶民字體) and immersive branding (沉浸式品牌). The Archaeological Museum of Piraeus adds monumental bronze casting (青銅鑄造), with the bronze Athena and a tragic mask, Geometric (幾何風格) and black-figure (黑繪) vases, and stelae crowned by palmettes (棕櫚葉飾): a compact history of Greek ornament in a single port museum. Meeting local people (與在地人互動), from two Athenians on the street, was part of the journey too: travel is also learning from people, not only from buildings. At the University of Piraeus (比雷埃夫斯大學) we met Stelios, a student there, and shared lunch with him in the university cafeteria (大學餐廳), a first friendship in Greece.",
"zhText": "抵達雅典的前四天，把城市當成一層層疊起來的書來讀：哈德良圖書館的科林斯柱廊就在莫納斯提拉基地鐵站旁，奧林匹亞宙斯神殿展現羅馬尺度的古典柱式；憲法廣場的總統衛隊交接是一場編舞，小主教座堂則把古老石雕再利用在牆上。中央市場的手寫價目卡、普西里的塗鴉與 Little Kook 主題立面，是最生動的庶民字體與沉浸式品牌。比雷埃夫斯考古博物館的青銅雅典娜、悲劇面具、幾何風格與黑繪陶瓶、棕櫚葉飾墓碑，一館看盡希臘裝飾史。也在比雷埃夫斯大學認識了學生 Stelios，在學生餐廳共進午餐。",
