{
"n": 6,
"folder": "06 義大利 2026-01-31 阿爾貝羅貝洛蘑菇屋與巴里",
"iso": "IT",
"country": "義大利",
"countryEn": "Italy",
"zh": "阿爾貝羅貝洛蘑菇屋與巴里",
"en": "Alberobello Trulli & Bari",
"date": "2026-01-31",
"photoRange": "2026-01-31",
"loc": "alberobello",
"xy": [
-1.603,
-6.006
],
"photoCount": 18,
"ready": true,
"enText": "The trulli (蘑菇屋) of Alberobello (阿爾貝羅貝洛), a UNESCO World Heritage Site, are a striking case of vernacular architecture (風土建築). They are built by dry-stone construction (乾砌石構造), without mortar: thick whitewashed (石灰粉刷) walls carry conical roofs made of corbelled (疊澀) limestone slabs, each ring stepping slightly inward until the cone closes. A carved pinnacle (屋頂尖飾) often crowns the top, and many roofs carry symbols painted in white lime, religious, astrological or protective signs that work like a vernacular sign system (符號系統); an information board explains their meanings. Seen from above, the clustered cones form a repetitive, almost modular townscape (模組化聚落). The trullo form is also used in larger buildings, as the church interior shows. In the afternoon in Bari (巴里), the narrow lanes of the old town and a Baroque (巴洛克) church façade show a contrasting southern Italian urban tradition of stone, light and ornament. The trulli show how local material, climate and construction method together produce a strong regional identity.",
"zhText": "阿爾貝羅貝洛的蘑菇屋（Trulli，世界遺產）是風土建築的經典：不用灰漿的乾砌石構造，厚厚的石灰白牆上，用石灰岩片一圈圈向內疊澀收成圓錐屋頂，頂端再加上雕刻尖飾。屋頂上用白灰畫的宗教、星象與護身符號，像一套民間的符號系統。從高處看，成群的圓錐屋頂形成近乎模組化的聚落。下午到巴里，舊城窄巷、仿羅馬式鐘樓與巴洛克教堂立面，呈現南義另一種石、光與裝飾的城市傳統。",
