"photoCount": 12,
"ready": true,
"enText": "The medieval town of Toruń (托倫), birthplace of Nicolaus Copernicus and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is one of the best-preserved Brick Gothic (磚造哥德式) towns of the Hanseatic world. Brick Gothic developed around the Baltic, where good building stone was scarce: walls, towers and churches are built of red brick, and ornament is created through brick itself. Stepped gables (階梯山牆) are decorated with blind niches (盲龕), recessed panels that give rhythm and shadow without openings, and pointed windows are filled with tracery (花窗格) including rose motifs. The Leaning Tower (斜塔) and the city walls show the fortification system along the river. Inside churches, stained glass (彩繪玻璃) and Baroque (巴洛克) altars add colour and later layers. The Copernicus statue stands near the Town Hall. A steel truss bridge (鋼桁架橋) crosses the Vistula, and the Wozownia gallery's logo shows contemporary graphic design in the historic town.",
"zhText": "托倫是哥白尼的故鄉，也是漢薩同盟世界保存最好的磚造哥德式城鎮之一（世界遺產）。波羅的海一帶缺乏好石材，牆、塔、教堂都用紅磚砌成，裝飾也靠磚本身完成：階梯山牆上的盲龕帶來節奏與陰影，尖拱窗裡有玫瑰紋花窗格。斜塔與城牆是沿河的防禦系統，教堂裡的彩繪玻璃與巴洛克祭壇則是後來的色彩層次。橫跨維斯瓦河的鋼桁架橋，和 Wozownia 藝廊的標誌，讓老城也看得到當代設計。",
