"enText": "Several days in Kraków (克拉科夫) move from medieval square to Japanese design, folk art and plant form. The Main Square (中央廣場) centres on the Cloth Hall (紡織會館) with its Renaissance parapet attic (女兒牆) and St Mary's Basilica (聖母聖殿), a Brick Gothic (磚造哥德式) church with unequal towers and Veit Stoss's altarpiece. Arata Isozaki's Manggha Museum (曼加日本藝術科技博物館, 1994) has a wave-like roof (波浪屋頂) and showed product design (產品設計) and Japanese typography (日文字型設計). In Kazimierz (卡齊米日), balancing acrobat sculptures (特技人雕塑) hang from the Bernatek footbridge, and the Ethnographic Museum (民族誌博物館) presents folk art (民俗藝術), paper cut-outs (剪紙) and the UNESCO-listed Kraków Nativity scenes (克拉科夫耶誕馬槽). The Jagiellonian University Botanical Garden (雅蓋隆大學植物園), founded in 1783, adds glasshouses (溫室) and a library of natural form (自然形態), the source of much biomorphic design (生物形態設計). City, craft and nature appear here as one continuous design education. Meeting local people (與在地人互動), from locals in Kraków, was part of the journey too: travel is also learning from people, not only from buildings.",
"zhText": "在克拉科夫的幾天，從中世紀廣場一路走到日本設計、民俗藝術和植物形態。中央廣場的紡織會館有文藝復興式女兒牆，聖母聖殿是一高一低雙塔的磚造哥德式教堂。磯崎新設計的曼加日本藝術科技博物館（1994）有波浪屋頂，展出產品設計與日文字型設計。卡齊米日的伯納特克橋上懸著平衡特技人雕塑；民族誌博物館展出剪紙、民俗彩繪與列入世界遺產的克拉科夫耶誕馬槽。1783 年創立的雅蓋隆大學植物園溫室，則是一座自然形態的圖書館。",
